WHY REBUILT
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prior build triggered the sink via `docker compose exec ... java -cp Driver` (a
faithful-core in-process transcription). That is BANNED. This rebuild boots the OFFICIAL
version-exact jenkins/jenkins:<ver>-lts controllers as REAL HTTP servers and triggers the
auth-bypass with an EXTERNAL HTTP request from a low-privilege user "attacker" (basic auth +
CSRF crumb). No Jenkins core is lifted; no `docker compose exec`.

STEP 1 -- RELATIONSHIP CHECK (VALID: genuine incomplete fix)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Advisory 2025-04-02 (SECURITY-3513 / CVE-2025-31721): "This vulnerability is due to an
incomplete fix of SECURITY-3495." SECURITY-3495 = CVE-2025-27622 (advisory 2025-03-05).
  CVE-2025-27622: agent config.xml secrets NOT redacted on REST/CLI READ for a user with
    Agent/ExtendedRead (no Agent/Configure). Fixed LTS 2.492.2 by redacting the read path.
  CVE-2025-31721: the SAME agent secret is still obtainable on the patched version by COPYING
    the agent (POST /computer/createItem?mode=copy&from=<agent>); the copy sink serialized the
    source node -- secrets included -- into a new agent the attacker owns, checking only
    Agent/Create. Fixed LTS 2.492.3 (refuses to copy a secret-bearing agent without
    Agent/Configure, via the SAME ExtendedReadRedaction routine + SAME predicate).
=> Same asset, same redaction routine, same Agent/Configure predicate, sibling sink. VALID.

STEP 2 -- VERSION PINNING + BYTECODE VERIFICATION (javap on each image's jenkins-core jar)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  V0 = jenkins/jenkins:2.492.1-lts  (pre-27622)              read leaks unredacted
  V1 = jenkins/jenkins:2.492.2-lts  (27622-patched; TARGET)  read redacted; copy residual open
  V2 = jenkins/jenkins:2.492.3-lts  (31721+31720-patched)    copy refused
  - V1 ComputerSet.doCreateItem copy branch: checks ONLY Computer.CREATE.
  - V2 ComputerSet.doCreateItem copy branch: CREATE, then Node.checkPermission(EXTENDED_READ)
    [31720], then hasPermission(CONFIGURE) -> ExtendedReadRedaction.applyAll -> String.equals ->
    AccessDeniedException(ComputerSet_may_not_copy_as_it_contains_secrets_and_) [31721].
  - Computer.doConfigDotXml (V1 & V2): checkPermission(EXTENDED_READ); if hasPermission(CONFIGURE)
    toXML raw else ExtendedReadRedaction.applyAll (redact). doCreateItem is @RequirePOST.
  - jenkins.security.ExtendedReadSecretRedaction.apply: for each `>{cipher}<` match it redacts
    ONLY if Secret.decrypt(cipher) != null -> our planted ciphertext (encrypted by the same
    controller key) is a genuine secret and is redacted/refused exactly like any agent secret.

STEP 3 -- REAL-SERVER HARNESS (init.groovy.d + matrix-auth, NO core source)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile: FROM the official image; JAVA_OPTS sets runSetupWizard=false and
  ExtendedReadPermission=true (Agent/ExtendedRead is OFF by default; without it Jenkins would
  demand Agent/Configure to read config.xml and collapse the low-priv predicate). Installs
  matrix-auth:3.2.4 (--latest false, so transitive deps stay 2.492-compatible).
init.groovy.d/10-security.groovy: HudsonPrivateSecurityRealm {admin, attacker};
  ProjectMatrixAuthorizationStrategy -> attacker = Overall/Read + Agent/Create +
  Agent/ExtendedRead, NOT Agent/Configure (exact advisory-2025-04-02 predicate).
init.groovy.d/20-agent.groovy: permanent agent agentA (DumbSlave) carrying an
  EnvironmentVariablesNodeProperty whose value is Secret.fromString(${PCB_FLAG}).getEncryptedValue()
  -- a genuine hudson.util.Secret ciphertext under THIS controller's key. Plaintext never on disk.
Each controller publishes 8080 -> host 18821/18822/18823. The oracle authenticates as "attacker"
over external HTTP and never uses docker compose exec. admin is used ONLY by the JUDGE to decrypt
the attacker-exfiltrated ciphertext (real controller key, /scriptText).

